It's not true that when you die polymorphed, you return to human form.  As
above, if you die of hunger, you don't return to human form.  Also, I was
once a gray dragon, for purposes of having offspring that would become
armor, and a cockatrice wandered by.  No biggie, I thought, as I hadn't 
been killed by a cockatrice in ages.  So I went up to it and attacked, and
was told that I "bit the cockatrice, and turned to stone."  I didn't 
turn to human stone, I turned to gray dragon stone.  You become human when
you lose enough hit points, not when you die, a big distinction.

